%I A402362 #13 Nov 24 2026 03:46:22
%S A402362 2,3,5,11,13,19,31,73,109,113,199,283,463,467,661,1103,1109,1123,1129,
%T A402362 1321,1327,1621,1627,2803,2861,5869,5881,6373,6379,9859,9931,9949,
%U A402362 10337,10343,15797,15803,15809,15817,15823,23917,24077,24083,24091,24097,24103,24107,24109,24113,24121,24137,42751
%N A402362 Indices at which psi(x) - x reaches new record values, starting at x = 2, where psi(x) = Sum_{p^k <= x} log p is the 2nd Chebyshev or cumulative von Mangoldt function log(A014963).
%C A402362 Related to the Riemann Hypothesis and zeta function.
%C A402362 All entries are primes.
%C A402362 If we start at x = 0 or x = 1, the initial values 2 and 3 would not appear, since we have psi(x) - x = 0, -1, -1.3..., -1.2..., -1.5..., -0.9... for x = 0..5.
%H A402362 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev_function">Chebyshev function</a>, as of Sept. 2026.
%o A402362 (PARI) PSIL=List(0); {PSI(x)=for(k=#PSIL+1,x,my(n); listput(PSIL, PSIL[#PSIL]+if(isprimepower(k,&n),log(n))));PSIL[max(x\1,1)]}
%o A402362 L402362=List(2); {A402362(n)=while(#L402362<n,my(k=L402362[#L402362],m=PSI(k)-k); until(PSI(k++)-k>m,);listput(L402362,k));L402362[n]}
%Y A402362 Cf. A014963.
%K A402362 nonn,new
%O A402362 1,1
%A A402362 _M. F. Hasler_, Nov 22 2026
